   134	Finally, if `V=Y-g2^(-1)(B)` and `W=A2-B`, then `V->W` is finite etale of
   135	degree three.  The nonempty open `V` in integral `Y` is connected, so its
   136	monodromy action on the three sheets is transitive.
   137	
   138	## 3. Acyclic-branch monodromy contradiction
   139	
   140	For any `b in B`, henselian idempotent lifting applied to (2.5) splits the
   141	local rank-three algebra into rank-two and rank-one factors.  A unital
   142	finite-flat rank-one algebra over the local base is the base itself.  Thus the
   143	whole local complement group fixes the companion sheet and maps into one
   144	conjugate of `S2`; a generic component meridian maps to a transposition.
   145	
   146	Arzhantsev--Zaidenberg classify every reduced connected simply connected
   147	plane curve, hence (2.4), into two normal-form families.
   148	
   149	1. In the line/comb family, a connected nontrivial comb has complement group
   150	   `F_s x <h>`, where the spine meridian `h` is central.  Its image is a
   151	   transposition, and the centralizer of a transposition in `S3` is precisely
   152	   its order-two subgroup.  Therefore the entire monodromy image lies in an
   153	   intransitive `S2`.  The one-line degenerations give the same conclusion.
   154	2. In the weighted-cone family, positive weighted radial flow makes both the
   155	   global complement and every sufficiently small **punctured weighted
   156	   sublevel neighborhood** of the origin deformation retract onto the same
   157	   weighted link complement.  Ordinary Euclidean balls and weighted
   158	   sublevels are cofinal neighborhoods, so the global complement group is
   159	   the origin-local complement group.  The local companion splitting at the
   160	   origin therefore puts the whole global monodromy image in one intransitive
   161	   `S2`.
   162	
   163	These families exhaust (2.4).  In every case the global monodromy is
   164	intransitive, contradicting the transitivity of `V->W`.  The assumed strict
   165	intermediate field with `deg(g2)=3` cannot exist.
   166	
   167	## 4. Picard/Zariski--Main firewall
   168	
   169	On the affine survivor open `U=Y-R`, the reviewed funnel validly proves
